<%# The loops in flight, at the same edge as the subagent and usage sheets: all
    three are facts about the work this conversation has going, and a reader
    checking one is asking the same question as a reader checking another.

    Hidden while nothing is running (see Web::Loops#loop_rows, which hands over
    an empty list): a conversation that never started a loop gets no control
    for it, and the element stays in the page so the poll has somewhere to write
    when one begins. A finished loop is its own message in the transcript, so
    the panel does not need to be the place it is remembered.

    It is a `<details>` like the two sheets beside it, so it opens without a
    script and its panel hangs above the row instead of off the bottom of the
    page. The card inside moves on its own -- an iteration can take minutes and
    the numbers are written to a file in between -- so the body polls while it
    is open and never while it is closed: a closed panel is not a thing the
    reader is looking at, and a timer that kept asking would be one request
    every three seconds for the rest of the session. The mark on the toggle is
    outside the body that poll targets, so the same answer carries it as an
    out-of-band swap (see Web::Loops#loop_state_markup). -%>
<%- hidden = loops.empty? -%>
<details class="usage-sheet usage-sheet-loops" id="loop-sheet"<%= " hidden" if hidden %>>
  <summary class="usage-toggle" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.title")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.title")) %>">
    <%= usage_icon(:loop) %><span class="loop-label"><%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.toggle")) %></span><span class="loop-state" id="loop-state"><%= View.render("_loop_state", loops: loops) %></span>
  </summary>

  <div class="usage-panel" role="group" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.title")) %>">
    <p class="panel-title"><%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.title")) %></p>
    <div id="loop-sheet-body"
         hx-get="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/loops<%= h(token_query) %>"
         hx-trigger="every 3s [this.closest('details').open]"
         hx-swap="innerHTML">
      <%= View.render("_loop_rows", loops: loops) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
